#### 1. Introduction

The purpose of this study is to investigate the effects of different types of music on the mood of individuals. The study will involve a total of 100 participants, who will be randomly assigned to one of four different music groups. Each group will listen to a different type of music for a period of 30 minutes, and their mood will be assessed before and after listening to the music. The study will also include a control group, who will not listen to any music. The results of the study will provide insight into the effects of different types of music on mood and may have implications for the use of music therapy in various settings.

#### 2. Hypotheses

It is hypothesized that listening to different types of music will have different effects on mood. Specifically, it is predicted that listening to classical music will have a calming effect, while listening to upbeat pop music will have an energizing effect. It is also predicted that listening to nature sounds will have a relaxing effect, while listening to heavy metal music will have a negative effect on mood.

#### 3. Methodology

Participants: The study will involve a total of 100 participants, aged 18-65 years old. Participants will be recruited through advertisements and social media.

Procedure: Participants will be randomly assigned to one of four different music groups: classical, pop, nature sounds, or heavy metal. Each group will listen to a different type of music for a period of 30 minutes. Participants will be asked to complete a mood questionnaire before and after listening to the music. The control group will not listen to any music.

Data Analysis: The data will be analyzed using statistical software to determine the differences in mood between the different music groups. The results will be presented in the form of graphs and tables.

#### 4. Results

The results of the study are pending, as the study has not yet been conducted. However, based on previous research, it is expected that the study will provide valuable insights into the effects of different types of music on mood. The results may have implications for the use of music therapy in various settings, such as hospitals, nursing homes, and schools.

#### 5. Discussion

The results of the study will provide valuable insights into the effects of different types of music on mood. The study may also have implications for the use of music therapy in various settings, such as hospitals, nursing homes, and schools. The study's findings may also contribute to the development of personalized music therapy programs that are tailored to individual needs and preferences. Overall, the study has the potential to make a significant contribution to the field of music therapy and may improve the quality of life for individuals who benefit from music therapy interventions.</s>